# Autonomous Skill Ecosystem Optimizer (`autonomous-skill-ecosystem-optimizer`)

When `skill-evolve` (`self-evolving-skill-synthesizer`) scaffolds a new skill, promotes a script, or hot-patches a rule, the rest of the 295+ skill ecosystem must immediately know how to interoperate with the new capability without creating orphaned skills, dead links, or prompt bloat.

This skill provides the **`skill-optimize`** engine (`~/.local/bin/skill-optimize`), which runs automatically inside `skill-evolve` (and on-demand via `skill-optimize --full`) to keep every skill in the repository working together in lockstep.

---

## 1. Closed-Loop Auto-Optimization Pipeline

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A["skill-evolve (--scaffold / --promote / --hot-patch)"] --> B["skill-optimize --target <skill>"]
    B --> C["1. Token & Whitespace Compaction"]
    C --> D["2. Cross-OS (Win11/Linux) & HW Offload Auto-Injection"]
    D --> E["3. Bidirectional Semantic Mesh Wiring (Top-3 Related Skills)"]
    E --> F["4. Stale Reference & Syntax Audit (32-Thread)"]
    F --> G["5. Rebuild skill_ecosystem_graph.json + agy-cheatsheet + 3-CLI Sync"]
    G --> H["repo-auto-sync --checkpoint --push (GitHub)"]
```

---

## 2. What `skill-optimize` Optimizes Automatically

1. **Bidirectional Semantic Cross-Linking (`config/skill_ecosystem_graph.json`):**
   - Computes capability similarity (Jaccard + domain prefix weighting) across all installed skills in parallel (`ThreadPoolExecutor` across 32 threads).
   - Automatically links newly scaffolded or evolved skills to their top 3–4 closest sibling skills (`## Related & Interoperating Skills`) and connects them to `dynamic-repo-model-cheatsheet` (`agy-cheatsheet` / `cs`) and `dynamic-skill-router`.
2. **Cross-OS & Hardware Offload Auto-Enrichment:**
   - Scans new or modified skills for build/OS/GPU keywords (`bash`, `cmake`, `cargo`, `blender`, `adb`, `ffmpeg`, `pytest`, `/tmp/`) and automatically injects `windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge` parity notes if missing.
3. **Stale Reference & Syntax Self-Healing:**
   - Scans all `SKILL.md` files for stale references to deprecated/removed workflows and compiles all `scripts/*.py` files via `py_compile` to guarantee zero broken helpers.
4. **Prompt Token Compaction:**
   - Collapses redundant blank lines and enforces compact YAML frontmatter descriptions so Gemini 4 Argon's 32,768-token prompt cache remains stable (`>95%` cache hit rate).

---

## 3. CLI Usage (`~/.local/bin/skill-optimize`)

```bash
# Optimize a specific skill and wire it into the ecosystem (called automatically by skill-evolve)
skill-optimize --target <skill-name>

# Run a full-fleet 32-thread optimization pass across all 296+ skills (<0.4s)
skill-optimize --full
```

## Windows 10/11 & Cross-Platform CLI Interop (`windows-linux-cross-os-runtime-bridge`)
- **Cross-OS Deployment (`install.ps1` & `install.sh`):** `skill-optimize`, `skill-evolve`, `repo-auto-sync`, and `agy-cheatsheet` (`cs`) run natively on Windows 10/11 (`.cmd` shims in `$HOME\.local\bin`) and Linux.
